WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.520
Slow down a little bit 
on the crane shot at the start.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.550
Camera two, move back 
before we enter melody B.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.060
Let's check the final 
group shot before we start.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.030
Could we raise the volume on our voices more?

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.570
Please turn down the rhythm section a little.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.530
B-Project is standing by.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.420
Ten seconds to rehearsal.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:25.170
Nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three...

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.290
Okay, that's a wrap.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.730
Th-These are idols?

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.020
You came.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.970
You were watching.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.450
Hey, what did you think 
of our rehearsal just now?

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.620
Wasn't it the best?

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.750
The actual performance could be insane.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.840
Yashamaru-san!

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.100
Wait. What?

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.620
That was incredible.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.930
I look forward to the actual performance 
that's in just one more week.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.830
The program you're going 
to be on has lots of viewers,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:46.270
so B-Project will finally get 
to stand in the spotlight.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.120
Indeed.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.190
Everyone worked hard day and night.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.640
Yashamaru-san, you don't usually 
come to our rehearsals.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.980
Did something happen?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.690
Yeah, that's right.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.650
I have something to tell all of you.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.530
Can I have your attention, please?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:07.420
Starting today, a new A&R is 
going to be handling B-Project.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.790
Introduce yourself.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.550
I-I started working at 
Gandara Music just the other day.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.860
I'm Sumisora Tsubasa.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.550
Um... I look forward to working with you!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.470
Really? You're B-Project's 
first female staff member.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.390
You've come to a difficult place.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:32.300
You're rather cute, aren't you?

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:38.240
If you're B-Project's A&R, does that 
mean you're managing three groups?

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:39.610
What? Um...

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.490
Huh? Are you scared?

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.120
You'll be fine.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.160
Can this little girl really handle 
being an A&R, Yashamaru-san?

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.260
We're going to be training her, 
so try to go easy on her for a while.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.890
After all, the president specifically 
appointed her to be your A&R.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.670
The president did?

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.010
He chose this girl?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.100
Come on, boys. Try not to be too mean.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.680
We're not being mean.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.610
We're just expressing 
our affection for you, newbie.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.930
Why, hello. We appreciate 
your continued business.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.290
Huh? What are you...

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.950
What? Are you serious?

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.850
Give me one second.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.650
Boys, introduce yourselves to her.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.720
Well, I guess we should introduce—

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.790
Me, me!

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.250
I'm Osari Hikaru, the eye candy of MooNs.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.180
This is our musclebound idiot, Nome Tatsuhiro.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.630
Don't call yourself eye candy.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.340
That doesn't embarrass you?

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.460
Not at all.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.910
Okay, okay. Sorry they 
don't have any manners.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.140
It's fine.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:56.150
My name is Sekimura Mikado.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.520
I look forward to working with you. He's...

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.780
Onzai Momotaro.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.340
What's this? Is that all?

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.900
Your expression's stiff, too.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.240
Come on. Smile, smile.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.180
Stop that.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.090
Then there's our leader...

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.290
I'm Masunaga Kazuna.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:17.170
They call me the leader, 
but I'm not actually.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.730
I guess it's fine for now, though.

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:22.440
Together the five of us are MooNs.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.420
Nice to meet you.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.770
I-It's nice to meet you, too.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.430
We're next.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.210
Nice to meet you.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.930
I'm Kitakado Tomohisa.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.340
Come on, Ryuji. Introduce yourself.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.380
Korekuni Ryuji.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.950
Our group, Kitakore, is a two-man unit.

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:45.940
Nice to meet you.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.160
N-Nice to meet you.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.740
I'm Ashu Yuta!

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.910
I'm so happy to have a new A&R.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.910
I'll do my very best, and I look 
forward to working with you.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.750
I'm Aizome Kento.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.750
We'll probably be spending 
a lot of time together,

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.940
so if there's anything 
you don't know, just ask.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.880
Aizome-san, in that case...

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.880
Call me Kento.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.600
Quit hitting on every woman 
you see! It's annoying!

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.100
Yeah, but you don't have to kick me, idiot.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.600
Sex addicts don't understand words.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:20.560
What did you say?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.010
Don't fight, Gochin and Ken Ken.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.810
Come on, Gochin. It's your turn.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.850
Do I have to tell her my name?

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.570
She won't be able to remember 
all of ours, anyway.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:32.830
Gochin.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.200
Kaneshiro Goshi.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:41.170
The three of us make up THRIVE!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.170
<i>I-I can't do this...</i>

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:47.550
<i>I can't handle this exceedingly unique 
group of men who shine so brilliantly.</i>

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.920
<i>There's no way.</i>

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:54.250
What's up, Yashamaru-san? 
Why the long face?

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:54.830
What?

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.450
Is it because of your earlier phone call?

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:03.190
Actually...

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:08.440
Your appearance on the FMJ Song Festival 
you just rehearsed for was canceled.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.200
Sorry!

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.370
What?

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:18.700
Yashamaru-san, what's the meaning of this?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:21.080
Are you underestimating THRIVE?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:25.910
A performance on a live broadcast 
was our chance to promote ourselves.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.130
I even sacrificed sleep to work on this.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.550
You should be apologizing to my damaged skin.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:36.220
One of our agency's clients 
is returning to Japan on short notice.

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:39.850
I received orders to make room 
for him in our time slot.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:45.060
Including B-Pro, five of Gandara's 
artists were set to perform.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:47.820
And if one had to be forced out...

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.450
It had to be us?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.390
I refuse to accept this!

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:54.950
Why did we have to get knocked out 
like a bunch of billiard balls?

00:07:55.340 --> 00:08:00.320
You know how much money and time 
we put into this program, don't you?

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.970
Gandara Music put in just as much effort.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:09.210
But... I'm sorry this happened, guys.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.520
I wasn't strong enough.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.420
Maybe it can't be helped.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:17.720
Masunaga! Why are you acting 
like a good, little boy?

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.140
It's disappointing, but when you 
consider what's best for Gandara,

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.800
it's not even on the same scale.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.480
I guess that means it was the right 
decision for the record and TV companies.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:33.530
I hate to admit it, but we haven't 
achieved enough to argue with them.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.120
This is a heavy loss for us.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.370
You'll pay for this one.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.700
The president of Daikoku Productions?

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:47.710
Our agency handles Kitakore and MooNs.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.630
I-I look forward to working with you.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.250
You used to work at a CD shop, right?

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.810
I heard the president of 
Gandara personally hired you.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.470
Do you have some kind 
of powerful connections?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.510
No, it's not like that.

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:05.600
I was suddenly hired to work at Gandara.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.050
Really?

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:11.190
Yashamaru-san told me 
to work as an A&R for idols.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:15.610
I'd heard of Kitakore, 
MooNs, and THRIVE before.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:22.880
But I don't really understand what 
an A&R is actually supposed to do.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.460
From the record company's perspective,

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.270
an A&R is meant to nurture 
and develop artists.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.630
There's music production, of course, but 
sometimes they also function as a manager.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.380
Agency employees like myself 
depend on them, as well.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:40.010
I-I have that many responsibilities?

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:41.760
Welcome back.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:45.570
MooNs has an interview with 
<i>That's TV</i> in Harajuku.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.360
That's starting soon. You'd better hurry.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:49.080
Yes, sir.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.480
See you later.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.560
Atsushi-san, you might want to leave soon.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.320
Today, he's especially—

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:02.280
Hey, Shuji.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:06.000
Who do you think you are 
to wait at the car by yourself?

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:10.460
I was going to tell you 
he's in a really bad mood.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.960
He certainly is particularly spirited today.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.880
It's not surprising given what happened.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.430
Hurry up and get in.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:22.160
THRIVE, you have your regular recording 
session with <i>Toranomon Radio</i>.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.930
Take care, boys.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.570
Thanks for your work today.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:25.570
Thanks.

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:26.580
Thanks.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:31.660
Um, Yashamaru-san, I—

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:34.230
Tsubasa-chan, you'll be heading 
to the Hiroozaka Studio.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:37.760
I'll let you handle Kitakore's 
recording of their new song.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.880
What? All by myself?

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:43.370
That's right. After all, you're the A&R.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.290
Yashamaru-san, where are you going?

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:49.200
I have some grown-up things to take 
care of regarding the earlier incident.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.230
But what should I do?

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.790
I've already talked to the studio.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.860
You'll learn while you're on the job.

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:59.050
B-But...

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.440
Thanks for handling this.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.600
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.840
<i>A recording? A recording is, um...</i>

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:08.630
Tsubasa-kun.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:10.620
Yes, sir.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:14.730
Could you play Kitakore's 
new song for us, please?

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.690
Okay.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:25.530
Could you turn it up a little?

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.450
Okay.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.140
Thanks.

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:30.240
Um...

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.830
Your performance at the FMJ Song 
Festival was just canceled.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:38.960
After such a major incident, 
will you be able to record a song?

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.470
What do you mean?

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:43.910
The lyrics you'll be singing are delicate.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:45.550
Singing today might be difficult—

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.470
What?

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.900
I wish you wouldn't make fun of us.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.440
No matter what happens, we have to sing.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.940
S-Sorry.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:57.690
Hey, Ryuji. You don't 
have to put it that way.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.020
Tsubasa-chan is just trying 
to be considerate of us.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.680
Then remember this.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.450
We're professionals. We're not that weak.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.090
Understood. I'll be more careful.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:11.460
No, we're sorry. Right?

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:20.710
We haven't had staff who worried about 
our mental state before recording before.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.720
What?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.830
He means "thank you."

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:27.600
Hey, Tomo! That's enough talking, right?

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:29.350
I can't hear the music!

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:37.980
Huh?

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.450
Is something wrong?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:43.210
Oh, no. It's nothing.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:49.400
Good morning.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:50.490
Good morning.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:55.280
You're lucky to have Kitakore for 
your first recording, Tsubasa-chan.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.170
They never fight.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:00.320
Even starting at this hour, 
we probably go past the witching hour.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:01.460
Witching hour?

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.950
Do you two have haps after this?

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.090
Haps?

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.710
No. Let's take it slow.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.520
Witching hour? Haps?

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:15.260
What?

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.600
Why don't you sit down?

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:21.530
Huh?

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.740
Korekuni-san, you're not 
going in there with him?

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:30.200
No. Tomo records first, then I 
layer my voice on top of his.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:34.090
Can you sing the same way 
when you record separately?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.210
Are you making fun of us again?

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:39.410
Not at all!

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.870
That's not my intention at all!

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:47.290
Let's start by running through 
the whole thing from the top.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.130
<i>Okay.</i>

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:50.700
Running through from the top?

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:55.200
It means singing the whole 
thing from beginning to end.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:58.770
I see. Run through from the top!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:13:59.760
I get it now!

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:06.150
<i>Fragile like the stars</i>

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:20.420
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:28.930
<i>I want to protect that somehow 
sad and downcast smile</i>

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.950
<i>His powerful singing voice</i>

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:25.670
<i>makes it seem like power is welling 
up from deep inside his heart.</i>

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:35.930
<i>I just want to look at you</i>

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:48.970
Okay, good.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.500
Let's switch now.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.400
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.700
Good work for now.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:57.160
Good work.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.130
Yeah.

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:03.080
<i>Fragile like the stars</i>

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:07.590
<i>and sad like the moon</i>

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:17.330
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:19.270
<i>It's such a delicate and gentle sound.</i>

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:26.290
<i>I want to protect that somehow 
sad and downcast smile</i>

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:23.580
That's it. That's why 
Korekuni-san sings second.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:33.180
<i>I just want to look at you</i>

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:32.090
Your voices have become one.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:33.850
Oh?

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:42.050
You're doing great. Should we record 
the harmonizing parts, too?

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:42.690
<i>Okay.</i>

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:46.960
Incredible. The song's coming 
together piece by piece.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.270
You're right.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:54.850
Some artists only sing the main vocals, 
but we sing all the parts ourselves.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:16:04.090
<i>You're so far away it's absurd 
and so close it makes me sad</i>

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:10.820
<i>Even though you're right beside me</i>

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:19.120
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.120
Huh?

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.300
Let's do that part again.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.120
<i>Okay.</i>

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:30.450
<i>Even though you're right beside me</i>

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:38.480
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:48.860
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:43.560
<i>Why does something feel off?</i>

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:56.600
Excuse me, but which channel 
are Tomo's vocals coming in on?

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:57.990
<i>Channel three.</i>

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:00.880
Could we try that one more time?

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.000
<i>We've adjusted the audio balance.</i>

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:11.840
We're really stuck now.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.200
Let's try that again.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:43.090
<i>Even though you're right beside me</i>

00:17:43.090 --> 00:17:51.110
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:07.690
<i>Is this...</i>

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:16.440
Excuse me.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:19.690
There's something I want you to hear.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.340
Tsubasa-chan?

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:25.250
S-Sorry. I couldn't help myself.

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:26.450
<i>What is it?</i>

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:31.330
<i>It's okay. Keep talking.</i>

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:38.090
Um, I'm not sure how to put it,

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:45.850
<i>but your harmony seems 
to be trapped inside a cage.</i>

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.680
What?

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:51.350
It's fighting with the other sounds.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:55.610
No matter how hard your voices try, 
they can't get out.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:59.080
<i>It's like they're screaming for help.</i>

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:03.770
Are you trying to say the harmonizing 
melody is dissonant during the chords?

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:05.570
What?

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:10.510
They're totally dissonant right here.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:16.420
Who made this elementary mistake?

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:18.240
Let's fix this right away.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:19.330
Yes.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.420
Um...

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.690
Tsubasa, could you get us some coffee?

00:19:22.690 --> 00:19:23.300
What?

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.430
Once we drink it, we'll resume recording.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:28.680
Okay.

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:42.200
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:52.310
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:06.200
<i>This... This is Kitakore's music.</i>

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.350
Good work.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.900
Good work.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.020
Good work.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.730
I'm going to call Yashamaru-san.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.060
I'm surprised.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:22.580
She seems to have no musical knowledge.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:26.990
But she identified the 
dissonance we didn't notice.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:34.370
Maybe Tsubasa belongs here.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.990
I'm exhausted.

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:48.050
But this is my new job.

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:51.500
My job as an A&R.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:52.820
Tsubasa.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.560
I had them copy the song over.

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:01.320
It's right out of the oven.

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:12.540
Kitakado-san, Korekuni-san, I was actually 
afraid of B-Project and its idols.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:16.460
I didn't understand why 
you shone so brightly.

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:20.190
But after this recording 
experience, I understand now.

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:23.970
The way you shine is absolutely necessary.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:29.270
The music born from Kitakore's 
brilliance is like magic.

00:21:29.270 --> 00:21:33.730
It sent my heart and body to another world.

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:37.270
Thank you for today.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.980
I'm relieved you seem more 
useful than I thought.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:45.490
Me, too. I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:49.530
I-I didn't actually think that.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:54.420
I've never seen you like this before, Ryuji.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:56.470
Tomo!

00:21:56.470 --> 00:21:57.650
Sorry, sorry.

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:02.300
Now let's listen to the song again.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:03.920
Okay.

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:14.140
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:32.800
<i>I want to protect that somehow 
sad and downcast smile</i>

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:39.690
<i>I just want to look at you</i>

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:47.500
<i>Unable to even make casual remarks</i>

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:51.210
<i>The dice land on one again</i>

00:22:51.210 --> 00:22:57.660
<i>I can't move forward like I want to</i>

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:05.580
<i>You're so far away it's absurd 
and so close it makes me sad</i>

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:12.200
<i>Even though you're right beside me</i>

00:23:12.550 --> 00:23:20.510
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:30.860
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:39.330
What is this?

00:23:40.030 --> 00:23:41.490
She's probably exhausted.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:01.000
<b>The BAD END Isn't So Bad</b>

00:23:55.620 --> 00:23:57.520
Let's meet in our dreams 
to pick up where we left off.

00:23:57.520 --> 00:23:59.550
Good night, my Cinderella.
